# AgentService: a curated service for agents with its own request budget and error masking (srv/agent-service.cds:
# @remote.budget, @remote.maskBackendErrors). The same reads and the same action through CatalogService are not
# limited and keep the backend's text. The MCP requests of AgentService are in MCP.http.
# Users (package.json, cds.requires.auth): alice is admin.

@server = http://localhost:5005/odata/v4/agent
@catalog = http://localhost:5005/odata/v4/catalog
@auth = Basic alice:alice


### Within the budget of the service (6 requests, 40 rows): the orders with their customer names, two systems
GET {{server}}/Orders?$select=ID,Title,CustomerName&$orderby=ID&$top=5
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Within the budget of the entity (5 rows): three customers
GET {{server}}/Customers?$select=ID,CustomerName&$orderby=ID&$top=3
Authorization: {{auth}}

### Every customer: the customer system answers 8 rows, more than @remote.budget.rows of AgentService.Customers (5):
### 502 REMOTE_BUDGET_EXCEEDED naming the annotation
GET {{server}}/Customers?$select=ID,CustomerName
Authorization: {{auth}}

### The same read through CatalogService, which the apps use: no budget of the agent service, every customer
GET {{catalog}}/Customers?$select=ID,CustomerName
Authorization: {{auth}}

### A refusal of the customer system through AgentService: masked, "The backend system could not process the request
### (reference ...)" with the backend's status; the text is in the consumer log under the reference
POST {{server}}/setCustomerStatus
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ID": "C002", "Status": "Z" }

### The same refusal through CatalogService: the backend's text, "Status must be 'A' or 'B'"
POST {{catalog}}/setCustomerStatus
Authorization: {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ID": "C002", "Status": "Z" }
